<p>Why would the foundation <strong>do</strong> these things?</p>
<p>Faced with an apparent duplication, why would it assume some kind of infiltration? The CIA might be paranoid, the FBI might be incompetent, but the foundation can't afford to have unclear motives or sloppy reasoning - and they know it.</p>
<p>Who on the O5 or ethics committee is stupid enough to think torture is a way to get information? The foundation is cold as marble, but it isn't cruel, and it doesn't do pointless things on the off-chance that &quot;Oh well, it might give us information, of some kind, somehow&quot;.</p>
<p>The premise is a good one - an old sci-fi staple. And the dialogue is snappy, and I think quite believable. I suggest it would be better as a foundation tale about an investigation into how the affair was mishandled.</p>

							</div>

								
					
